<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Doubles results on the fifth day of</p>
<p>the French Open tennis tournament on Friday.</p>
<p>Prefix number denotes seeding</p>
<p>Mixed doubles first round:</p>
<p>Helena Vildova (Czech Republic)/Filippo Messori (Italy) beat</p>
<p>Nana Miyagi (Japan)/Greg Van Emburgh (U.S.) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Kimberly Po (U.S.)/Rikard Bergh (Sweden) beat Arantxa  Sanchez</p>
<p>Vicario (Spain)/Mansour Bahrami (Iran) 6-1 6-3</p>
<p>Magalie Lamarre/Olivier Delaitre (France) beat Elena Wagner</p>
<p>(Germany)/Sander Groen (Netherlands) 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania)/Leander Paes (India) beat Rene</p>
<p>Simpson (Canada)/Jim Grabb (U.S.) 6-2 6-0</p>
<p>Laura Montalvo/Lucas Arnold (Argentina) beat Ginger Helgeson</p>
<p>Nielsen/Jack Waite (U.S.) 7-5 6-4</p>
<p>Karine Quentrec-Eagle/Rodolphe Gilbert (France) beat Sandrine</p>
<p>Testud (France)/Paul Kilderry (Australia) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Lori McNeil/T.J. Middleton (U.S.) beat Clare Wood</p>
<p>(Britain)/Joshua Eagle (Australia) 6-3 7-5</p>
